      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1220",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Pimelodella gracilis (Valenciennes, 1835)</li><li><strong>Common names:</strong> Graceful Pimelodella, Schlanker Fadenwels (Germany)</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Corrientes, Río Paraná, Argentina.</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 170 mm (6.7 in) SL</li><li><strong>IUCN Red List:</strong> Least Concern (last assessed 2018)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1220",
      "html": "<p>South America: Orinoco, Amazon and La Plata basins. Collected in Arroyo Tropa Vieja, Salinas, Uruguay.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1220",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.5 - 7.8</li><li>Temperature: 20.0-24.0°C (68-75.2°F)</li><li>dH: 5-20</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1220",
      "html": "<p>In nature feeds on worms and insects.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1220",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
